<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10928"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Km<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Km<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 11:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why was Bill Butterworth&#39;s van found four blocks away at the McDonald&#39;s since he was supposed to be doing some work for them that day.  Why didn&#39;t he park it at house?  Why would someone park four blocks away to walk to a house where the murder victims were.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
