<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10939"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 12:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Butterworth&#39;s van was found at a McDonald&#39;s seven blocks from the Fager home. <BR> <BR>Evidence showed that on Dec. 30 Butterworth took money from an ATM and bought shirts at Montgomery Ward&#39;s. <BR> <BR>The Fagers&#39; missing silver 1983 VW Rabbit was found in the hotel parking lot where Butterworth was arrested. <BR> <BR>he stated he blacked out after seeing them, can&#39;t remember going to ATM etc.... <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10939-->
<!--Post: 12424--><!--Time: 1112210269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12424"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 11:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just joined the bill butterworth -shudder in wichita yahoo group. I will post interesting tidbits as i read the posts over there. I think this is a btk case. <BR> <BR>Anyone got info on the letter Mrs Fager rec&#39;d? <BR> <BR>Return address &#34;William Thomas Killman&#34; <BR>did William Thomas kill man? and denny killed the little girls? This is so frustrating, not knowing if the dna left near the girls was tested against anything other that butterworth. <BR> <BR>The morning of the crime, Mr Fager went to meet with a plumber at his rental property. We all know Denny&#39;s bro is a plumber. Anyway to find out if he was the plumber? <BR> <BR>I dont know yet if the little girls were murdered while their dad was gone, or after he got back home.  more later <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12424-->
<!--Post: 12427--><!--Time: 1112211910-->
