<!--/Post: 12427-->
<!--Post: 12439--><!--Time: 1112228104-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12439"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 4:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found something else on the same yahoo group, that really needs to be verified.  The post was dated 3/7/05.  The person wants to know if Rader and Mr. Fager knew each other since they were both at Butler comm. college and both majoring in business.  I have no idea if this is true.   <BR> <BR>Also, I found out Butterworth&#39;s full name is WILLIAM THOMAS Butterworth.  The return address of Bill Thomas Killman seems a little more like a clue now.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12439-->
<!--Post: 12472--><!--Time: 1112277921-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12472"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 6:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree Tulip, bill thomas killman, maybe that is dennys way of admitting, or at least teasing, that he did this.   <BR> <BR>denny did go to butler, but i have read different times, some news sources put it before the airforce, and others say he went there after the service.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12472-->
<!--Post: 12475--><!--Time: 1112283271-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12475"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 7:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Paul Fecteau &#40;sp&#41; who is writing a book on the Fager case posted: <BR> <BR>DNA receives no mention at any time in the trial or in the news <BR>articles about the case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12475-->
<!--Post: 12570--><!--Time: 1112464367-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12570"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 9:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hopefully, the police will include Mrs. Fager in reviewing the mementos that BTK collected. They will be very remiss if they do not. Bondage, strangling, posing: all signatures of BTK and all three present at the Fager homicides.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12570-->
<!--Post: 12653--><!--Time: 1112689383-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12653"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 1:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why would BTK respond to this murder and not the dozens of other brutal murders in Wichta over the years. I think the reasons are the same as the Bright murder it didnt go well. Also that WPD closed the case like they were sure the husband did it in the Wegerle case is very bone headed.Butterworths story is way more believable than the case against him .DNA didnt match Butterworth they had skin in the Wegerle case and did nothing. How can I beleive that any one but BTK is responsible for the Fagers what a shame .<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12653-->
<!--Post: 12656--><!--Time: 1112702898-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12656"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 5:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well said Superbike!!!  I agree 100%. They should not me closed minded about any of the unsolved cases. <BR> <BR>Denny confesses to some, but he wants to save the others for a few years down the road, when he is lonely and rotting in his cage. He will call some bigshot in under the ruse of wanting to confess, and then we find out more. If nothing else, the man is the most patient game player I have ever heard of. I really believe he quit doing so much of his game, under some feeling of obligation to his kids, he had to get them grown up, and he looked forward to that day so he could come back out and play.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12656-->
<!--Post: 12664--><!--Time: 1112715346-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12664"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 8:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty: I think that you are right. He always has an ace in the hole, and he still has everybody playing the game to his liking. Yes, the fact that he commented on this particular case and voiced &#39;admiration&#39; for the killer tells something. After all BTK is his own and only best fan. He will use even murdered people for leverage. Though never planning to get caught, I do believe that he envisioned scenarios should he be id&#39;d. Always keeping something back is a good way to stay alive alittle longer. Bundy tried it. Ridgway plead out just to give resolution to the families. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12664-->
<!--Post: 12666--><!--Time: 1112717233-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12666"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 9:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree, Itty, about the game-playing and why he dialed it back. There is this perverse combination of wannabe Ward Cleaver and meatcleaver-wielding killer in him. <i>&#40;I know he was a strangler, just liked the play on words.&#41;</i> I don&#39;t mean to be silly, but it reminds me of that movie where Kathleen Turner played the perfect suburban mommy who was also a serial killer. It&#39;s the way other Dads give up drawing or painting or something, then take it up on retirement, as my own father did. Denny just had a far deadlier and dark pursuit he set aside.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12666-->
<!--Post: 12761--><!--Time: 1113060245-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12761"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 09, 2005 - 8:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Anyone know the name of the hotel Butterworth was arrested at and what town in Florida?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12761-->
<!--Post: 12764--><!--Time: 1113060813-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12764"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 09, 2005 - 8:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No. But I can&#39;t see why that would be significant, either. People, killers or not, rarely choose things for the arcane and symbolic reasons fiction would have us believe. Some killers aren&#39;t even sophisticated enough intellectually to think with such depth. To me, murder almost never implies a <i>deep</i> psyche. Knowing what hotel Butterworth was in when arrested to me is as significant as knowing what make and model of truck Denny was driving when he was arrested. Since we do know he was in a Park City Compliance Officer vehicle, it&#39;s almost moot otherwise. I will say that the vehicle he was driving at Home Depot was signficant, only because the plates were traced to him. So, I guess I&#39;m wondering, why do you want to know this about the hotel? <BR> <BR>For the record, Beattie said that Butterworth knew no one in Florida and Butterworth said he didn&#39;t even know why he ended up there. I think he was just trying to get away from that triple murder thing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12764-->
<!--Post: 12775--><!--Time: 1113157301-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12775"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 10, 2005 - 11:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR>This is why I ask. Why was BB&#39;s car parked at McDonald&#39;s? Coincidentally, there was a novel written by John D. MacDonald, entitled &#34;The Executioners&#34; MacDonald died on December 28th, 1986, almost exactly a year before the Fager murders. <BR> <BR>A movie &#34;Cape Fear&#34; &#40;1962&#41;was based on that novel. In the movie Max Cady tells Bowden that after he got out of prison, he took his ex-wife away for about 3 days, and made her write a letter, which he planned to use as blackmail if she told her new husband what he did. He terrorized Bowden&#39;s family of three. You&#39;d have to see the movie. <BR> <BR>Maybe there was a reason he picked the hotel he stayed at even if he didn&#39;t remember why. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12775-->
<!--Post: 12776--><!--Time: 1113158158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12776"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 10, 2005 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s a link to John D. MacDonald info <BR><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_D._MacDonald" target=_top>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_D._MacDonald</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12776-->
<!--Post: 12782--><!--Time: 1113197689-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12782"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 10, 2005 - 10:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR>Just to add something else, Cady &#40;Mitchum&#41;said he was in prison for 8 years, 4 months, and 13 days. 8413. 843 was Nancy Fox&#39;s address, except there&#39;s &#34;no one&#34; like in the movie Bloodwork. Also, Bowden&#39;s &#40;Peck&#41; daughter&#39;s name was Nancy. <BR> <BR>This is the 1962 version of the movie.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
